+
+/*
+ * THE STYLE WHEN THERE IS NO VIEW, which is the only way a cell can get one.
+ *
+ * graphicsStyle is a category on NSView, so a cell asking [controlView graphicsStyle] gets nil the
+ * moment it is drawn without a view, and every bezel, arrow and check mark after that is a message
+ * to nil: silent, no drawing, no error. AppKit draws into the CURRENT CONTEXT and does not need a
+ * view for any of it, and applications rely on that -- LibreOffice draws its check boxes with
+ * inView:nil, which is why they had no box. Cells call this instead.
+ */
+NSGraphicsStyle *NSGraphicsStyleForView(NSView *view);
